  "note": "What a fence thinks one item is worth, in credits (D-125). The worth is the cheapest honest price of the item where one exists (the cities' shelves and the regional exchange), so a fence, who pays at most 60 percent of it, never pays more than the item costs to buy. Items with no worth here are not bought at all: nothing a person can come by for free (stone, logs, dirt) and nothing worthless (paper, bread). Goods with no honest price at all (fence-only goods: what burglars find in homes and offices, D-144) are listed under fence_only; a fence may pay more of their worth (up to 80 percent with the Thief skills) because nothing honest can be undercut by them.",
